---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import benchmark from '../../data/signal-triage.json';
import {
  evaluateStream,
  hhmmFromWindow,
  specimenVerdict,
  type Clauses,
  type SpecimenPost,
  type StreamMeta,
  type StreamRow,
} from '../../utils/signal-triage';
import { photoSrcset, photoTiers } from '../../utils/photo-src';
import '../../styles/enforcement-gates.css';
import '../../styles/signal-triage.css';

// Case study: public-post signal triage and outage detection on a synthetic
// public-chatter benchmark. All posts and timestamps come from
// src/data/signal-triage.json, deterministically generated by
// scripts/signals/evaluate.py (seed 11). Nothing here comes from an employer,
// platform vendor or customer stream.
const pageTitle = 'Public-Signal Triage and Outage Detection';
const description = 'Boolean query gates, burst detection and a structured brief: separating early outage witnesses from public noise before an official status update.';

const HERO = 'gv-1fd48bd9';
const hero = photoTiers(HERO);

const meta = benchmark.meta as StreamMeta;
const rows = benchmark.rows as unknown as StreamRow[];
const specimens = benchmark.specimens as SpecimenPost[];
const rawSeries = benchmark.ungated_series as number[];
const stages = benchmark.stages;

const defaultClauses: Clauses = { prox: true, excl: true, corr: true, dedup: true };
const gated = evaluateStream(rows, meta, defaultClauses);
const ungated = evaluateStream(rows, meta, { prox: false, excl: false, corr: false, dedup: false });

const pct = (v: number, d = 1) => `${(v * 100).toFixed(d)}%`;
const fmt = (v: number) => v.toLocaleString('en-US');

// SVG timeline geometry (viewBox 640 x 216, zero inline styles).
const TL = { w: 640, h: 216, l: 36, r: 16, top: 28, bottom: 184 };
const plotW = TL.w - TL.l - TL.r;
const plotH = TL.bottom - TL.top;
const maxCount = Math.max(...rawSeries, 24);
const stepX = plotW / meta.windows;
const barW = Math.max(4, stepX - 3.5);
const yOf = (count: number) => TL.bottom - (Math.min(count, maxCount) / maxCount) * plotH;
const hOf = (count: number) => (Math.min(count, maxCount) / maxCount) * plotH;
const xCenter = (w: number) => TL.l + w * stepX + barW / 2;
const tickWindows = [0, 6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 35];
const yTicks = [0, 5, 15, 25].filter((v) => v <= maxCount);

const BENCHMARK_SHA256 = '07d9d448addf4f301a8ffd022d93c72fbe1dfb6a2018afd72851588cff80402b';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: pageTitle,
  description,
  datePublished: '2026-11-24',
  dateModified: '2026-11-24',
  url: 'https://thejohndwilliams.com/work/signal-triage/',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'John D. Williams', url: 'https://thejohndwilliams.com' },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={description}
  ogImage="/og/pages/work.jpg"
  ogImageWidth={1200}
  ogImageHeight={630}
  lcpImage={HERO}
  lcpImageSizes="100vw"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)}></script>

  <section class="enf-hero relative flex items-end overflow-hidden" data-hero-under>
    <picture>
      <source type="image/avif" srcset={photoSrcset(HERO, 'avif')} sizes="100vw" />
      <source type="image/webp" srcset={photoSrcset(HERO, 'webp')} sizes="100vw" />
      <img
        src={`/images/photography/hero/${HERO}.webp`}
        width={hero.hero.w}
        height={hero.hero.h}
        alt="Glass tower rising into the night"
        class="sig-hero__img absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
        data-bleed-short
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </picture>
    <div class="hero-scrim-left absolute inset-0"></div>
    <div class="enf-hero__lockup relative z-10 w-full px-6 sm:px-10 lg:px-20 pb-12 sm:pb-16 md:pb-24">
      <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3 sm:mb-4">Case study · Public signals</p>
        <h1 class="t-title mb-4 sm:mb-5 font-serif tracking-tight">{pageTitle}</h1>
        <p class="enf-deck">Boolean query gates, burst detection and a structured brief: turning noisy public posts into an early outage warning.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="enf-page sig-page" data-sig-page>
    <dl class="enf-meta">
      <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Personal project, synthetic benchmark</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Stream</dt><dd>{fmt(meta.posts_total)} posts, {meta.windows} windows</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Method</dt><dd>Release gates, Wilson 95% CI</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Published</dt><dd>November 2026</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <p class="enf-lede">
      On the benchmark stream, the gated query holds{' '}<span class="enf-num" data-sig-bind="precision">{pct(gated.precision)}</span>{' '}precision, cuts false alarms from{' '}<span class="enf-num">{ungated.fp}</span>{' '}to{' '}<span class="enf-num" data-sig-bind="fp">{gated.fp}</span>, and raises an early warning{' '}<span class="enf-num" data-sig-bind="lead">{gated.leadMinutes} min</span>{' '}before a status page updates.
    </p>

    <section class="enf-block">
      <p class="enf-step">01</p>
      <h2>Query gates before a rule ships</h2>
      <p>Monitoring public posts fails in the opposite direction of a lab classifier: an analyst writes a broad keyword rule to avoid missing an event, and the feed drowns in casual idioms, scheduled maintenance notices, commentary reshares and copy-pasted spam. Once an alert channel cries wolf twice in a shift, people mute it.</p>
      <p>Every collection query here is treated as code with a release gate. Before a query enters production alerting, it must clear {pct(meta.precision_gate, 0)} precision and {pct(meta.recall_gate, 0)} recall on a labelled evaluation stream, with zero pre-fault false pages.</p>

      <figure class="sig-console enf-wide" data-sig-console data-sig-state="ships">
        <div class="sig-console__live" data-sig-live hidden>
          <div>
            <span class="sig-k">Collection clauses (toggle to test the release gate)</span>
            <div class="sig-clauses" role="group" aria-label="Query filter clauses">
              <span class="sig-clause sig-clause--locked">Anchor terms (locked)</span>
              <button type="button" class="sig-clause" data-clause="prox" aria-pressed="true">Proximity NEAR/6</button>
              <button type="button" class="sig-clause" data-clause="excl" aria-pressed="true">Negative exclusions</button>
              <button type="button" class="sig-clause" data-clause="corr" aria-pressed="true">First-hand corroboration</button>
              <button type="button" class="sig-clause" data-clause="dedup" aria-pressed="true">Shingle deduplication</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="enf-readout">
            <div class="enf-stat">
              <p class="enf-stat__k">Precision</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__v" data-sig-bind="precision">{pct(gated.precision)}</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__sub" data-sig-bind="precisionCI">{pct(gated.wilson[0])} to {pct(gated.wilson[1])}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="enf-stat">
              <p class="enf-stat__k">Recall</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__v" data-sig-bind="recall">{pct(gated.recall)}</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__sub" data-sig-bind="recallSub">{gated.tp} of {meta.signal_total} true reports</p>
            </div>
            <div class="enf-stat">
              <p class="enf-stat__k">False alarms</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__v" data-sig-bind="fp">{gated.fp}</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__sub" data-sig-bind="preFault">0 pre-fault pages</p>
            </div>
            <div class="enf-stat">
              <p class="enf-stat__k">Warning lead</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__v" data-sig-bind="lead">{gated.leadMinutes} min</p>
              <p class="enf-stat__sub" data-sig-bind="detectAt">Fires {gated.detectTime} UTC</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sig-verdict" aria-live="polite">
            <span class="sig-k">Release gate verdict</span>
            <p class="sig-verdict__v" data-sig-decision>Query ships</p>
            <ul class="sig-verdict__reasons" data-sig-reasons>
              {gated.reasons.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span class="sig-k">Illustrative stream specimens under active clauses</span>
            <ul class="sig-specimens">
              {specimens.map((sp) => {
                const v = specimenVerdict(sp, defaultClauses);
                return (
                  <li class="sig-specimen" data-specimen={sp.id} data-verdict={v.kind}>
                    <span class="sig-specimen__meta">{sp.time} · {sp.region}</span>
                    <p class="sig-specimen__text">{sp.text}</p>
                    <span class="sig-specimen__tag" data-specimen-tag>{v.label}</span>
                  </li>
                );
              })}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sig-table-wrap">
          <table class="enf-table sig-stages">
            <caption class="enf-cap vg-cases__cap">Cumulative clause performance across the {fmt(meta.posts_total)}-post synthetic stream.</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Query stage</th>
                <th scope="col">Precision (95% CI)</th>
                <th scope="col">Recall</th>
                <th scope="col">False alarms</th>
                <th scope="col">Gate</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {stages.map((s) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">{s.label}</th>
                  <td>{pct(s.precision)} ({pct(s.wilson[0])} to {pct(s.wilson[1])})</td>
                  <td>{pct(s.recall)}</td>
                  <td>{s.fp} ({s.pre_fault_alarms} false {s.pre_fault_alarms === 1 ? 'page' : 'pages'})</td>
                  <td class:list={[{ 'sig-stages__blocked': !s.ships }]}>{s.ships ? 'Ships' : 'Blocked'}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <p>Lexical precision alone is still vulnerable to coordinated copy-paste bursts: fifteen identical credit-spam posts carrying realistic symptom words pass proximity, exclusion and corroboration rules at 02:00 UTC, firing a false alarm fifteen minutes before any fault exists. Text-shingle deduplication collapses the burst to one uncorroborated cluster and restores the gate.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="enf-block">
      <p class="enf-step">02</p>
      <h2>Indications and warning before status confirmation</h2>
      <p>Volume alone is a brittle trigger. The burst rule requires at least {meta.burst_min_count} distinct corroborated reports in each of two consecutive {meta.window_minutes}-minute windows across at least {meta.burst_min_regions} regions. In the benchmark, a regional outage starts at {meta.fault_utc} UTC, crosses the multi-region burst gate at {gated.detectTime} UTC, and precedes the simulated status-page update at {meta.status_ack_utc} UTC by {gated.leadMinutes} minutes.</p>

      <figure class="sig-burst enf-wide">
        <svg
          viewBox={`0 0 ${TL.w} ${TL.h}`}
          class="sig-burst__svg"
          data-sig-svg
          data-max-count={maxCount}
          role="img"
          aria-label={`Five-minute post volume from ${meta.start_utc} to ${meta.end_utc} UTC. Ungated anchor hits spike before the fault; gated corroborated reports stay below threshold until the ${meta.fault_utc} UTC fault and fire an early warning at ${gated.detectTime} UTC, ${gated.leadMinutes} minutes ahead of status confirmation.`}
        >
          {yTicks.map((v) => (
            <g>
              <line x1={TL.l} x2={TL.w - TL.r} y1={yOf(v).toFixed(1)} y2={yOf(v).toFixed(1)} class={v === meta.burst_min_count ? 'sig-burst__threshold' : 'sig-burst__grid'} />
              <text x={TL.l - 8} y={(yOf(v) + 3).toFixed(1)} text-anchor="end" class="sig-burst__tick">{v}</text>
            </g>
          ))}

          {rawSeries.map((raw, w) => {
            const gCount = gated.winCounts[w];
            const x = TL.l + w * stepX;
            const isTrigger = gated.detectWindow !== null && (w === gated.detectWindow || w === gated.detectWindow - 1);
            return (
              <g>
                <rect x={x.toFixed(1)} y={yOf(raw).toFixed(1)} width={barW.toFixed(1)} height={hOf(raw).toFixed(1)} class="sig-burst__raw" />
                <rect x={x.toFixed(1)} y={yOf(gCount).toFixed(1)} width={barW.toFixed(1)} height={hOf(gCount).toFixed(1)} class:list={['sig-burst__gated', { 'is-alert': isTrigger }]} data-sig-bar={w} />
              </g>
            );
          })}

          <line x1={xCenter(meta.fault_window).toFixed(1)} x2={xCenter(meta.fault_window).toFixed(1)} y1="18" y2={TL.bottom} class="sig-burst__marker" />
          <text x={xCenter(meta.fault_window).toFixed(1)} y="13" text-anchor="end" dx="-4" class="sig-burst__label">Fault {meta.fault_utc}</text>

          {gated.detectWindow !== null && (
            <g>
              <line x1={xCenter(gated.detectWindow).toFixed(1)} x2={xCenter(gated.detectWindow).toFixed(1)} y1="18" y2={TL.bottom} class="sig-burst__marker sig-burst__marker--alert" />
              <text x={xCenter(gated.detectWindow).toFixed(1)} y="13" text-anchor="start" dx="4" class="sig-burst__label sig-burst__label--alert">Alert {gated.detectTime}</text>
            </g>
          )}

          <line x1={xCenter(meta.status_ack_window).toFixed(1)} x2={xCenter(meta.status_ack_window).toFixed(1)} y1="28" y2={TL.bottom} class="sig-burst__marker" />
          <text x={xCenter(meta.status_ack_window).toFixed(1)} y="25" text-anchor="start" dx="4" class="sig-burst__label">Status {meta.status_ack_utc}</text>

          {tickWindows.map((w) => (
            <text x={xCenter(w).toFixed(1)} y={TL.h - 10} text-anchor="middle" class="sig-burst__tick">{hhmmFromWindow(w, meta.window_minutes)}</text>
          ))}
        </svg>
        <ul class="sig-legend" aria-hidden="true">
          <li class="sig-legend__item"><span class="sig-swatch sig-swatch--raw"></span>Ungated anchor hits</li>
          <li class="sig-legend__item"><span class="sig-swatch sig-swatch--gated"></span>Gated signal</li>
          <li class="sig-legend__item"><span class="sig-swatch sig-swatch--alert"></span>Burst gate triggered</li>
        </ul>
        <figcaption class="enf-cap"><span>Five-minute buckets across {meta.windows * meta.window_minutes / 60} hours. Dashed line marks the {meta.burst_min_count}-report per-window threshold.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="enf-block">
      <p class="enf-step">03</p>
      <h2>Separating reporting from judgment</h2>
      <p>Detection is half the job; the other half is briefing decision-makers without overstating noisy public reporting. The alert roll-up separates what people reported from the assessment, pairs likelihood with an explicit confidence level, and names the collection gaps that could overturn the call.</p>

      <figure class="sig-brief enf-wide">
        <div class="sig-brief__head">
          <span class="sig-brief__stamp">ILLUSTRATIVE · SYNTHETIC BENCHMARK</span>
          <span class="sig-brief__stamp">ISSUED 02:26 UTC · T+11 MIN</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sig-brief__grid">
          <div class="sig-brief__cell sig-brief__full">
            <span class="sig-k">Bottom line up front (BLUF)</span>
            <p>We assess it is <strong>likely</strong> that a checkout and login failure is affecting customers in the Central and Coast regions as of 02:15 UTC, based on corroborated first-hand public reports.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sig-brief__cell">
            <span class="sig-k">Underlying reporting</span>
            <p>Eleven deduplicated posts between 02:15 and 02:25 UTC cite failed logins, 502 errors and payment timeouts across the Central and Coast regions, clearing the two-window multi-region burst gate (baseline: 0.3 per window).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sig-brief__cell">
            <span class="sig-k">Analytic confidence</span>
            <p class="sig-brief__conf">Moderate confidence</p>
            <p>Witnesses independently describe the same symptoms across two regions, but public posts self-select for affected users and internal monitoring has not yet confirmed a root cause.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sig-brief__cell">
            <span class="sig-k">Alternative hypothesis</span>
            <p>A fault at an outside payment provider could produce identical checkout failures for customers in those regions without any failure in the app itself.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sig-brief__cell">
            <span class="sig-k">Indicators and collection gaps</span>
            <p>Confidence rises to High if internal error rates or synthetic checks confirm the regional boundary; the assessment is falsified if reports stay confined to customers of a single payment provider.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="enf-block enf-reqs">
      <p class="enf-step">04</p>
      <h2>Requirements I would set</h2>
      <ol class="enf-req-list">
        <li><span class="enf-req__n">1</span><p><strong>Gate every query on precision and recall before it alerts.</strong> A collection query is production logic; no Boolean rule ships without clearing held-out thresholds and Wilson lower-bound checks.</p></li>
        <li><span class="enf-req__n">2</span><p><strong>Deduplicate before counting volume.</strong> One actor pasting fifteen copies is one observation, never a fifteen-sigma event.</p></li>
        <li><span class="enf-req__n">3</span><p><strong>Require multi-window, cross-region corroboration to page a human.</strong> Requiring persistence across two windows filters transient blips while preserving twenty-plus minutes of warning lead.</p></li>
        <li><span class="enf-req__n">4</span><p><strong>Separate probability from analytic confidence in every brief.</strong> High likelihood on thin reporting is still low or moderate confidence, and decision-makers need both numbers.</p></li>
        <li><span class="enf-req__n">5</span><p><strong>State what would falsify the assessment.</strong> Naming the indicator that disproves the call prevents early hypotheses from hardening into confirmation bias during a live event.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="enf-block enf-method">
      <p class="enf-step">05</p>
      <h2>Method and provenance</h2>
      <p>The benchmark stream holds {fmt(meta.posts_total)} synthetic posts ({meta.signal_total} true disruption reports and {fmt(meta.posts_total - meta.signal_total)} background idioms, planned-maintenance notices, commentary echoes and coordinated copy-paste bursts) generated deterministically in Python at seed {meta.seed}. Every figure and table on this page computes directly from that JSON file; no employer, customer or third-party platform records are used.</p>
      <p class="sig-prov">Artifact: src/data/signal-triage.json · seed {meta.seed} · sha256 {BENCHMARK_SHA256}</p>
      <p class="enf-code"><a href="https://github.com/thejohndwilliams/thejohndwilliams-site/blob/main/scripts/signals/evaluate.py" class="link-draw" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Benchmark generator and gate evaluator</a></p>
      <p class="enf-return"><a href="/work/">Back to the work</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <script src="../../scripts/signal-triage-console.ts"></script>
</BaseLayout>
